    <channel>
        <title>Clippy</title>
        <link>https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Harman206/clippy-updates/main/appcast.xml</link>
        <description>Clippy — always-on macOS assistant. Update feed.</description>
        <language>en</language>

        <!--
            Each ship appends a NEW <item> at the TOP.

            scripts/release.sh (in the source repo) emits a ready-to-paste
            snippet with the right EdDSA signature and file length once the
            notarized zip is built. Sparkle uses the signature to verify the
            zip wasn't tampered with — without a matching EdDSA signature the
            install is refused.

            For the initial entry below we deliberately publish no <enclosure>.
            Sparkle sees that sparkle:version matches what's installed and
            stops without attempting a download, so the missing URL never
            gets requested. This is how 0.1.1 users see "You're up to date"
            on every check until 0.2.0 lands.
        -->

        <item>
            <title>Version 0.1.1</title>
            <pubDate>Sun, 17 May 2026 12:57:26 +0000</pubDate>
            <sparkle:version>0.1.1</sparkle:version>
            <sparkle:shortVersionString>0.1.1</sparkle:shortVersionString>
            <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>14.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
            <description><![CDATA[
                <ul>
                    <li>Backend reliability: env-newline trimming, Azure audio API pinned, multipart fix, GPT-5 sampling-param sanitisation, GREATEST(0,…) for Postgres.</li>
                    <li>Whisper transcription locked to English (no accent-driven Hindi/Marathi drift).</li>
                    <li>Notch dismiss: race fix, dismiss-suppression window, follow-up Fn-ask clears stale answers.</li>
                    <li>Sign-in error: tap-to-dismiss + 6s auto-dismiss.</li>
                    <li>Keychain service rename + file-first read so adhoc-signed builds stop popping keychain prompts.</li>
                    <li>3-layer identity guardrails (input pre-filter + system prompt + output filter).</li>
                </ul>
            ]]></description>
        </item>

    </channel>
</rss>
